  "_id": "6682bd5eba0e94a3c4025c34",
  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be the feet of perpendiculars from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math> respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∠</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is a right angle, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to ________</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Equation of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Now, let any point on the above line be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Similarly, for line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p>So, any point on the above line will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, the direction ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now, finding foot of perpendicular from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math> using perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Hence, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And similarly, the direction ratio of </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>And again, finding foot of perpendicular from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math> using perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Also, given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⊥</mo><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now, using perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
